<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - April 11.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - April 11.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 04/11/97  04/04/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East		8.81     10.78     3.79	 4.64	3.5</p>
<p>West	     45.25     46.61    17.46	17.99     29.5</p>
<p>Total Canada   54.06     57.39    17.46	11.67     17.7</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 04/11/97: 232.55 bcf, 04/04/97: 232.55 bcf.</p>
<p>West capacity 04/11/97: 259.11 bcf, 04/04/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
